* tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_sim_ready.spice -- auto-generated by
* script/gen_chip_sim_ready_v9.py, from:
*   /sessions/dreamy-ecstatic-heisenberg/mnt/TR-1um_Async_I2C/schematic/tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v9_lvs.spice
* (the LVS-confirmed-clean chip netlist, RING_OSC excluded -- see
* this script's own module docstring for why the source file already
* excludes RING_OSC with no manual stripping needed). Mechanical
* fixes applied on top of the verbatim source, all required for a
* real ngspice run (none change electrical intent):
*   1) all 358 bare M-line transistor instances -> X-line
*      (subckt-call) form, so ip62_models' PMOS/NMOS .subckt wrappers
*      resolve them (KLayout's own bare-M LVS convention doesn't).
*   2) 45 bracket-vector net names (146
*      occurrences, e.g. tx_data[0] -> tx_data_0), everywhere they
*      appear -- a general SPICE-portability cleanup (kept even after
*      #3 below turned out to be the real fix for the "too few nodes"
*      error; harmless and arguably still worth having).
*   3) 2 malformed comment-continuation line(s) in the
*      i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm PININFO block (bare "+" -> "*+") --
*      THIS was the actual root cause of a real local ngspice run's
*      "too few nodes" error on the x2 instantiation, found by
*      comparing this file's two multi-line PININFO comment blocks
*      against each other; see module docstring fix #3 for the full
*      diagnosis.
*   4) 4 diode instance parameter(s) renamed A=/P= ->
*      AREA=/PJ= (DD1/DD2 inside OSS_ESD_5V_DIO) -- ngspice's native
*      diode instance parser doesn't accept the short forms KLayout's
*      LVS writer emits; values unchanged, purely a keyword-spelling
*      fix. Found from a real local ngspice run's "unknown parameter
*      (a)" error past fix #3 above; see module docstring fix #4.
*   5) 4 bare-M devices (originally model=NMOSE, all inside
*      the OSS_ESD_5V_* pad-ESD cells) renamed to model=MNE -- NMOSE is
*      a KLayout DRC/LVS device-recognition label with no SPICE-library
*      counterpart; MNE is ip62_models' extended-drain NMOS and what
*      these cells' own source xschem schematic actually specifies
*      (property model=MNE) -- see module docstring for the full
*      cross-check. This is the best-supported mapping found but IS
*      an inference; sanity-check ESD-cell nodes on first real run.
* DO NOT hand-edit -- regenerate instead.

** tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v9_lvs.spice -- chip-level LVS reference netlist (v9)
** Generated by script/gen_lvs_spice_top_v9.py from:
**   1) schematic/i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm_v9.spice (core, LVS-clean per
**      design_notes.md 77.47 -- "Congratulations! Netlists match.")
**   2) simulations/OSS_FRAME_GIO.spice (GIO pad-ring frame, transistor
**      level, from its own xschem schematic)
**   3) schematic/gio_connections.json (GIO<->core connection map,
**      derived + cross-verified in design_notes.md 78.1/78.4)
** x1 = OSS_FRAME_GIO, x2 = i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm, matching the
** instance naming already used in the (now-stale, pre-v9)
** src/tr_1um_i2c_slave_async.cir. Nets prefixed NC_ are genuinely
** unconnected on both sides (spare pads P9/P10/P11-in/OUT2/OUT7/OUT9/
** OUT10/OUT15, and core's tx_data_1/rx_valid/addr_match/rw/busy --
** none of these are wired to any GIO pad in this design, confirmed by
** gio_connections.json's own "core_outputs_not_connected_to_any_pad"
** and per-terminal "unconnected" notes) -- each gets its own unique
** floating net name rather than being tied together, so LVS sees them
** as independently floating, matching the real chip.
**
** TOP-LEVEL PIN FIX (this revision): the top subckt now declares its
** 16 real bond-pad ports explicitly (P1-P7, VSS, P9-P15, VDD -- P8
** does not exist in this frame). The previous revision had a
** port-less ".subckt tr_1um_i2c_slave_async" line, matching the old pre-v9
** src/tr_1um_i2c_slave_async.cir's own structure -- and the
** LAYOUT-side extraction of the same top cell independently confirmed
** the same gap (src/tr_1um_i2c_slave_async.extracted:
** ".SUBCKT tr_1um_i2c_slave_async VSS", only one top pin). Neither
** side exposed the chip's real bond-pad nets as actual top-level
** PORTS, which is what let KLayout's LVS pin/port alignment fall back
** on ambiguous internal matching and produced the OSS_FRAME_GIO-level
** pin mismatches (HIZ2/HIZ7/HIZ9/HIZ10/HIZ15/OUT13) seen in
** src/LVS_error.lvsdb. Fix: rename each pad's carrying net to the
** pad's own canonical name (e.g. P1's net was "IN5") and declare all
** 16 as real subckt ports; see design_notes.md for the full writeup.

