* 2026-09-02 fix (design_notes.md section 108.14): these 8 MUX2 "hold"
* (B) inputs were wired to `rx_data_r_N`, a net that is NEVER driven
* anywhere in this file (a dead naming artifact distinct from the real,
* port-connected DFFRB Q output `rx_data_N`) -- confirmed via grep, see
* 108.9/108.10/108.13's investigation trail. The intended behavior (per
* the RTL: `rx_data_r` holds its value on every scl_gated edge except the
* one where `is_last_bit`/`_087_` selects the freshly-shifted byte) needs
* a genuine self-feedback path (B tied to the flop's OWN Q), which was
* simply missing -- on every one of the 7 non-load edges per byte (and
* on every subsequent edge for the rest of the transaction, since
* scl_gated keeps toggling long after the byte is captured), the DFFRB's
* D input floated and got re-clocked with whatever indeterminate charge
* sat on the dangling node, corrupting the just-captured value. Fixed by
* wiring B to the real `rx_data_N` Q output instead, giving each bit a
* proper static hold.
