** 2026-09-02 MANUAL SIMULATION-ONLY PATCH (design_notes.md section 108.20):
** shreg_0..shreg_6 の7段DFFRBは元々 _156__row3 を共有していたが、
** _156__row3 は同時に rx_data_1..7 用DFFRB 7段も駆動しており、
** 合計14個のDFFRB CKピンを1個のBUF_X1で駆動する過負荷状態だった
** （一方 last_bit_pending が使う _156__row1 は9負荷、_156__row2は
** 1負荷、_156__row0 に至っては負荷ゼロで完全に未使用だった）。
** この負荷差がrow1とrow3の間に構造的・決定論的なクロックスキュー
** を生み、last_bit_pending の0→1遷移が引き起こす大きな同時
** スイッチング（_087_・rx_valid・phase系ロジックへの広いファン
** アウト）と、shregの捕獲エッジがちょうど際どく重なることで、
** shregの"1"を保持していたビットだけが崩壊する現象（108.19）を
** 引き起こしていたと判断した。
** 対策として、shregの7段DFFRBだけを、完全に未使用だった
** _156__row0 に付け替え、rx_data系（7負荷）・shreg系（7負荷）を
** 分離した。これによりrow3の負荷は14→7に半減し、shregは
** last_bit_pendingが乗るrow1からもrx_dataが乗るrow3からも独立
** した専用クロックバッファを持つことになる。DFFRB STDCELL自体
** および他のネットには一切手を加えていない。
x_530_ VDD _192_ sda_in_row2 shreg_0 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
x_531_ VDD _189_ shreg_0 shreg_1 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
x_532_ VDD _190_ shreg_1 shreg_2 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
x_533_ VDD _193_ shreg_2 shreg_3 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
x_534_ VDD _191_ shreg_3 shreg_4 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
x_535_ VDD _218_ shreg_4 shreg_5 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
x_536_ VDD _194_ shreg_5 shreg_6 _016_ GND _156__row0 DFFRB
** 2026-09-02 MANUAL SIMULATION-ONLY PATCH (design_notes.md section 108.4/
** 108.5): DEL1-based sda_d replaced with a transparent latch (MUX2 +
** self-feedback on B/Y), matching the v6 RTL fix in src/i2c_slave_async.v.
** DEL1's fixed ~2ns delay could not reliably detect stop_pulse's SDA
** rising edge (RC-limited via the external pull-up, measured ~15-20ns
** here) -- confirmed via script/gen_chip_tb_batch14_v9.py's fine-grained
** STOP1 trace (busy_clr peaked at only ~0.05V, never reaching a valid
** digital level). This netlist-only patch is for simulation verification
** of the fix; the real layout/synthesis flow (yosys -> dedup_gates.py ->
** insert_row_buffers.py -> insert_bufth_scl_sda.py -> gen_lvs_spice_v9.py
** -> ... -> gen_chip_sim_ready_v9.py) still needs to be re-run from the v7
** RTL to produce a layout-accurate netlist (same caveat as section 106's
** own manual .CK() patches).
** v7 UPDATE (design_notes.md section 108.6/108.7): the first cut of this
** patch (scl_row2 & rst_n gated latch) fixed the cold-start case but not
** the recurring case -- a real bus idles with SCL held continuously HIGH
** between a STOP and the next START (no obligation for SCL to ever go
** low during idle), so a latch gated purely by scl never re-arms after
** STOP and misses the following START (confirmed via i2c_slave_async_
** tb.v regression). Fixed by gating a second stage with `busy` instead:
** while busy=0 (idle, including through reset via busy_clr's own ~rst_n
** term) sda_d is forced to 1 regardless of scl; only while busy=1 (a
** transaction is underway, scl toggles every bit) does sda_d follow the
** scl-gated transparent latch. Since busy clears the instant stop_pulse
** fires, sda_d re-arms immediately with no dependency on scl ever going
** low again.
** v8 UPDATE (design_notes.md section 108.8): the v7 patch (two MUX2 gates
** wired back into each other) is a DYNAMIC latch -- confirmed via a real
** batch14 run that it does not hold reliably for the multi-microsecond
** durations needed here (addr_match/rx_data/read-byte all failed even
** though busy itself, a genuinely static NOR2 SR latch, still worked).
** Rebuilt with the same proven static (regenerative) SR-latch topology as
** busy/rst_scl_domain_held, generalized to a gated D-latch. See
** src/i2c_slave_async.v's v8 header comment for the full writeup.
xu_sda_target VDD sda_in_row2 busy VDD sda_target GND MUX2
xu_sda_lat_en VDD sda_lat_en busy scl_row2 GND NAND2
