xu_buf_scl_n_row1 VDD scl_n scl_n_row1 GND BUF_X1
** 2026-09-02 MANUAL SIMULATION-ONLY PATCH (design_notes.md section 108.22):
** sda_oe_r was sharing `scl_n_row0` with txreg_0/1/2 (4 DFFRB loads total
** on one BUF_X1). A wrdata trace showed sda_oe_r's D-input (_005_) settled
** to the correct new value (a "1") a full 5000ns ahead of its own capture
** edge, yet the DFFRB held its old "0" instead of capturing the "1" --
** the same qualitative symptom as the shreg collapse (108.19/108.20):
** a DFFRB failing specifically to capture a 0->1 transition, at a
** specific edge, while 0-holds and other edges on the same domain work
** fine. Unlike `_156_`, `scl_n` only had 2 row-buffer copies instantiated
** (row0, row2) with no idle spare to move to, so a new dedicated BUF_X1
** copy (`scl_n_row3`) is added here, and sda_oe_r alone is moved onto it
** (see x_528_ below), isolating its clock edge from txreg_0/1/2's shared
** buffer. No change to DFFRB itself or to any other net.
xu_buf_scl_n_row3 VDD scl_n scl_n_row3 GND BUF_X1
xu_bufth_scl VDD scl scl_buf GND BUFTH
xu_bufth_sda_in VDD sda_in sda_in_buf GND BUFTH
